      "body": "## Motivation\n\nOn gfx950 the extend-attention kernel only takes the 128-row query tile when `128 < head_dim <= 256`:\n\n```python\nelif _is_gfx95 and 128 < Lq <= 256:\n    BLOCK_M, BLOCK_N = (128, 64)\n    num_warps = 8\nelse:\n    BLOCK_M, BLOCK_N = (64, 64)\n    num_warps = 4\n```\n\nEvery workgroup in this kernel streams the whole prefix, so the KV bytes read per call scale with the number of query tiles: doubling `BLOCK_M` halves them. And `BLOCK_M / num_warps = 128 / 8 = 16` rows per warp is exactly one MFMA tile at `matrix_instr_nonkdim=16`, so the wider tile maps cleanly onto the hardware rather than leaving a partial tile.\n\nNeither part of that reasoning depends on the head dim being above 128. Head dims 64 and 128 — which cover most dense models, including the Llama family — are left on the narrow tile for no stated reason.\n\n## Modifications\n\nDrop the lower bound on the condition:\n\n```python\nelif _is_gfx95 and Lq <= 256:\n```\n\n`BLOCK_N` stays at 64 in both branches, so the KV sweep per query row is unchanged and each row's online-softmax accumulates in the same order. `BLOCK_M` only changes how many query rows a program handles, and rows are independent. The output is therefore expected to be bit-identical, and it is — see below. Other AMD architectures, CUDA, and head dims above 256 are untouched.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n**MI355X (gfx950), 256 CU, ROCm 7.2, torch 2.9.1, Triton 3.7.0.** `B=32, H_Q=64, H_KV=8`, bf16, causal, tensors from the repo's `_build_batch`.\n\n12 configurations, head_dim {64, 128, 256} × N_CTX {1024, 2048, 4096, 8192}, run before and after. Each run hashes its inputs as well as its `o_extend`, so the output comparison is only accepted when the inputs provably matched.\n\n**12/12 inputs identical, 12/12 outputs bitwise identical.**\n\n`test/registered/attention/unittests/dense/test_triton.py` and `.../swa/test_triton.py`: 14 passed, 2 skipped, 55 subtests passed.\n\n## Speed Tests\n\nMinimum over 7 repetitions of `triton.testing.do_bench(warmup=100ms, rep=500ms, return_mode=\"median\")`, one idle GPU. The baseline sweep was run twice, before and after the patched sweep; **maximum run-to-run drift was 0.33%**.\n\n### head_dim 64 — `BLOCK_M` 64 → 128\n\n| N_CTX | before (ms) | after (ms) | delta |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1024 | 0.4712 | 0.2588 | **−45.1%** |\n| 2048 | 1.8496 | 0.8606 | **−53.5%** |\n| 4096 | 5.9978 | 2.8041 | **−53.2%** |\n| 8192 | 16.8052 | 8.0892 | **−51.9%** |\n\n### head_dim 128 — `BLOCK_M` 64 → 128\n\n| N_CTX | before (ms) | after (ms) | delta |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1024 | 0.6572 | 0.5349 | −18.6% |\n| 2048 | 2.4469 | 1.8698 | −23.6% |\n| 4096 | 8.0976 | 6.2074 | −23.3% |\n| 8192 | 22.8645 | 17.4134 | −23.8% |\n\n### head_dim 256 — control, tile choice unchanged\n\n| N_CTX | before (ms) | after (ms) | delta |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1024 | 0.8084 | 0.8083 | −0.0% |\n| 2048 | 2.8070 | 2.8060 | −0.0% |\n| 4096 | 9.4010 | 9.3854 | −0.2% |\n| 8192 | 26.3511 | 26.3371 | −0.1% |\n\nAll four control rows are inside the 0.33% drift, as they must be — the condition change cannot reach this head dim.\n\n### Register pressure\n\nA wider query tile costs registers, and this file has a history of Triton 3.7 gfx950 spill regressions, so wall-clock alone is not enough. From the compiled AMDGCN at `N_CTX=4096`:\n\n| head_dim | sgpr_count | sgpr_spill | vgpr_count | vgpr_spill |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 64 | 105 → 106 | 4 → 2 | 107 → 114 | 0 → 0 |\n| 128 | 106 → 106 | 4 → 6 | 169 → 151 | 0 → 0 |\n| 256 | 106 → 106 | 14 → 14 | 227 → 227 | 0 → 0 |\n\nNo VGPR spills appear at any head dim, the SGPR spill counts stay in the single digits and move in both directions, and head_dim 128 actually uses 18 fewer VGPRs on the wider tile. Nothing here resembles the scratch-spill regime that motivated the narrower tile for `Lq == 576`.\n\n## What this does not cover\n\ngfx950 only, and kernel-level only — no end-to-end serving numbers. The change is gated on `_is_gfx95`, so no other architecture is affected by construction.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #37891933533](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37891933533)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37891933281](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37891933281)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37891933484](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37891933484)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
